From: bringup <bringup@t1100.local>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: t1100: enable CONSYS and the MT6631 Wi-Fi HIF

Patch 0049 described the SoC side of the MT6631 combo but left both nodes
disabled: nothing was allowed to touch the connectivity hardware before the
first power-on test.  That test is now planned, and the tablet runs the
second developer's kernel (6.12.114-g400cb6f-touch-rot) whose display, touch
and RAM work is already verified, so the risk of probing CONSYS on boot is
bounded and a rollback image exists.

Both nodes become status = "okay":

  consys@18070000   wmt_drv.ko probes, walks the CONN power domain through
                    the SPM register it maps itself and leaves the chip
                    powered off until the WMT ioctl asks for it
  wifi@180f0000     wlan_drv_gen3.ko probes only when the module is loaded
                    (the vendor stack is built out-of-tree), so "okay" here
                    just makes the HIF described, not started

Nothing else changes: no clock, regulator, address or IRQ is touched.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6771-fplus-t1100.dts
@@ -936,7 +936,7 @@
 		vcn33_bt-supply = <&mt6358_vcn33_reg>;
 		vcn33_wifi-supply = <&mt6358_vcn33_reg>;
 
-		status = "disabled";
+		status = "okay";
 	};
 
 	/*
@@ -973,6 +973,6 @@
 		clocks = <&infracfg CLK_INFRA_CQ_DMA>;
 		clock-names = "wifi-dma";
 		hardware-values = <0x788 0xa5800 0xa5800>;
-		status = "disabled";
+		status = "okay";
 	};
 };
